On platforms like RISC-V that do not support MCJIT,
Mesa uses ORC JIT instead.
However, it does not add it to the list of LLVM modules,
and in turn, that causes undefined reference issues when building with a static LLVM,
because the corresponding static libraries are not linked.

See https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/work_items/16445

Patch taken from https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44521

From 50ffce8eb83a4bf7dd1e529127b04fabd8106acf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:25:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] llvmpipe: do not call LLVMLinkInMCJIT() when using OrcJIT

Obviously LLVMLinkInMCJIT() call wouldn't be needed when using OrcJIT,
however it's mostly a no-op and currently the mcjit LLVM module is
wrongly linked instead of orcjit.

Remove the call when using OrcJIT, to remove the dependency to the mcjit
LLVM module.

Backport-to: *
Signed-off-by: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c | 2 ++
 src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_screen.c    | 8 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c
index f5b6110f9120..e3c7c4336dee 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c
@@ -311,11 +311,13 @@ lp_build_init(void)
       return true;
 
 
+#if !GALLIVM_USE_ORCJIT
    /* LLVMLinkIn* are no-ops at runtime.  They just ensure the respective
     * component is linked at buildtime, which is sufficient for its static
     * constructors to be called at load time.
     */
    LLVMLinkInMCJIT();
+#endif
 
    lp_init_env_options();
 
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_screen.c
index 80f60f19c2be..34b7dac17981 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_screen.c
@@ -897,10 +897,14 @@ lp_disk_cache_create(struct llvmpipe_screen *screen)
    char cache_id[BLAKE3_HEX_LEN];
    _mesa_blake3_init(&ctx);
 
-   if (!disk_cache_get_function_identifier(lp_disk_cache_create, &ctx) ||
-       !disk_cache_get_function_identifier(LLVMLinkInMCJIT, &ctx))
+   if (!disk_cache_get_function_identifier(lp_disk_cache_create, &ctx))
       return;
 
+#if !GALLIVM_USE_ORCJIT
+   if (!disk_cache_get_function_identifier(LLVMLinkInMCJIT, &ctx))
+      return;
+#endif
+
    _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, &gallivm_perf, sizeof(gallivm_perf));
    update_cache_blake3_cpu(&ctx);
    _mesa_blake3_final(&ctx, blake3);
-- 
